### 9. Potential Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|------|----------|------------|
| Race condition on `logs` storage key from concurrent writes | Low | Serialized promise chain in SW; content/popup send via message (also serialized by SW's single-threaded message handling) |
| Service worker terminated during log write | Low | `writeEntry` promise chain handles rejections silently; individual log entries are lossy by design |
| Content script loads before logger.js (load order in manifest) | Medium | Manifest `js` array guarantees load order; verified by Chrome documentation |
| `importScripts('logger.js')` fails if file path wrong | Medium | File is at extension root, same directory as background.js; MV3 service worker `importScripts` paths are relative to extension root |
| Popup log viewer causes popup to exceed reasonable height | Low | Log list has `max-height:180px` with overflow scroll; toggle is collapsed by default |
| Log messages contain characters that break HTML | Low | `esc()` function already exists in popup.js and handles `&<>"'` |
| `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` in content.js for logs could trigger the "Could not establish connection" error if SW is terminated | Low | The `catch` block on `sendMessage` and the `chrome.runtime.lastError` check in the callback both handle this silently |
| Confusion between `cycleStores`'s existing `log` array variable and the new `log` logger variable | Low | Renamed the existing variable to `cycleLog` |

